{"route":"/docs/4.5/layout/utilities-for-layout/","version":"4.5","renderedVersion":"4.5","title":{"id":"content","type":"heading","en":"Utilities for layout","level":1},"lead":{"id":"page--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"<a href=\"https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/blob/v4.5.3/site/docs/4.5/layout/utilities-for-layout.md\">View on GitHub</a>"},"blocks":[{"id":"content--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"For faster mobile-friendly and responsive development, Bootstrap includes dozens of utility classes for showing, hiding, aligning, and spacing content."},{"id":"changing-display","type":"heading","en":"Changing <code>display</code>","level":2},{"id":"changing-display--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use our <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/utilities/display/\">display utilities</a> for responsively toggling common values of the <code>display</code> property. Mix it with our grid system, content, or components to show or hide them across specific viewports."},{"id":"flexbox-options","type":"heading","en":"Flexbox options","level":2},{"id":"flexbox-options--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Bootstrap 4 is built with flexbox, but not every element’s <code>display</code> has been changed to <code>display: flex</code> as this would add many unnecessary overrides and unexpectedly change key browser behaviors. Most of <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/components/alerts/\">our components</a> are built with flexbox enabled."},{"id":"flexbox-options--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"Should you need to add <code>display: flex</code> to an element, do so with <code>.d-flex</code> or one of the responsive variants (e.g., <code>.d-sm-flex</code>). You’ll need this class or <code>display</code> value to allow the use of our extra <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/utilities/flex/\">flexbox utilities</a> for sizing, alignment, spacing, and more."},{"id":"margin-and-padding","type":"heading","en":"Margin and padding","level":2},{"id":"margin-and-padding--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Use the <code>margin</code> and <code>padding</code> <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/utilities/spacing/\">spacing utilities</a> to control how elements and components are spaced and sized. Bootstrap 4 includes a five-level scale for spacing utilities, based on a <code>1rem</code> value default <code>$spacer</code> variable. Choose values for all viewports (e.g., <code>.mr-3</code> for <code>margin-right: 1rem</code>), or pick responsive variants to target specific viewports (e.g., <code>.mr-md-3</code> for <code>margin-right: 1rem</code> starting at the <code>md</code> breakpoint)."},{"id":"toggle-visibility","type":"heading","en":"Toggle <code>visibility</code>","level":2},{"id":"toggle-visibility--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"When toggling <code>display</code> isn’t needed, you can toggle the <code>visibility</code> of an element with our <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/utilities/visibility/\">visibility utilities</a>. Invisible elements will still affect the layout of the page, but are visually hidden from visitors."}],"demos":[],"nav":[{"en":"Getting started","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Introduction","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/getting-started/introduction/"},{"en":"Download","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/getting-started/download/"},{"en":"Contents","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/getting-started/contents/"},{"en":"Browsers & devices","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/getting-started/browsers-devices/"},{"en":"JavaScript","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/getting-started/javascript/"},{"en":"Theming","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/getting-started/theming/"},{"en":"Build tools","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/getting-started/build-tools/"},{"en":"Webpack","href":"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/4.5/getting-started/webpack/"},{"en":"Accessibility",